From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samu Kaarlela <samu@Samus-MacBook-Pro.local>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 17:56:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] ui/egl-helpers: Fix build with integer
 EGLNativeDisplayType

The native_display parameter of eglGetPlatformDisplayEXT() is void *,
but qemu_egl_get_display() passes EGLNativeDisplayType. That is a
pointer on X11/GBM, but an int on other platforms, e.g. with ANGLE's
eglplatform.h on macOS. Building on macOS with CONFIG_X11 (set whenever
pkg-config finds x11, as with Homebrew's libx11) therefore fails:

  ui/egl-helpers.c: error: incompatible integer to pointer conversion
  passing 'EGLNativeDisplayType' (aka 'int') to parameter of type
  'void *' [-Wint-conversion]

Convert explicitly through uintptr_t, which is correct for both
pointer and integer display types.
---
 ui/egl-helpers.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ui/egl-helpers.c b/ui/egl-helpers.c
index 3530bd9..b58bfb2 100644
--- a/ui/egl-helpers.c
+++ b/ui/egl-helpers.c
@@ -608,7 +608,8 @@ EGLDisplay qemu_egl_get_display(EGLNativeDisplayType native,
     /* In practise any EGL 1.5 implementation would support the EXT extension */
     if (epoxy_has_egl_extension(NULL, "EGL_EXT_platform_base")) {
         if (platform != 0) {
-            dpy = eglGetPlatformDisplayEXT(platform, native, NULL);
+            dpy = eglGetPlatformDisplayEXT(platform,
+                                           (void *)(uintptr_t)native, NULL);
         }
     }
 
